sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant SDB@{ "type" : "database" } as Sender DB
    participant S as Sender
    participant R as Receiver
    participant RDB@{ "type" : "database" } as Receiver DB

    Note over S,R: A new unidirectional synchronisation<br> stream is opened

    S->>R: VERSIONS(supportedVersions)

    loop While acknowledgements are queued
        S->>SDB: generateAck(contactId, maxMessageIds)
        SDB-->>S: ACK(messageIds)
        S->>R: ACK(messageIds)
        R->>RDB: Mark acknowledged messages as seen
    end

    loop While messages are eligible for transmission
        S->>SDB: generateBatch(contactId, capacity, maxLatency)
        SDB-->>S: Collection of messages

        loop For every message in the batch
            S->>R: MESSAGE(groupId, timestamp, body)
            R->>R: Validate record and derive messageId
            R->>RDB: Store message or update existing message
            R->>RDB: Queue ACK for sender
        end
    end

    S->>R: End of stream
    Note over S,R: The simplex outgoing session closes when<br> no records remain

    opt Later reverse-direction simplex session
        R->>S: VERSIONS(supportedVersions)
        R->>S: ACK(messageIds)
        R->>S: End of stream
        S->>SDB: Mark messages as seen by receiver
    end